<title>USA: Standard Management to redeem preferred shares.</title>
<headline>Standard Management to redeem preferred shares.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Standard Management Corp, a finanical services holding company, said Friday it was calling for redemption all outstanding shares of its class S convertible cumulative redeemable preferred stock.</p>
<p>The redemption date is August 1 and the redemtion price is $10 plus accrued dividends of $1.6274 a share, the company said.  </p>
<p>The preferred stock trades on the Nasdaq Small Cap Market under the symbol &quot;SMANP.&quot;</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
</text>
